{#-
  AgentGym training/serving chat template, Llama 3 header format.

  Structurally identical to agentgym_chat_template.jinja (the ChatML one used for Qwen);
  only the turn delimiters differ. Keeping the two in lockstep is the point: the
  second-base-model arm exists to test whether the specialization/generalization trade-off
  is a property of agent post-training or a property of Qwen3-8B, and that comparison is
  only clean if the prompt construction, the loss masking and the stop-token handling are
  the same on both sides.

  The two deliberate properties carried over:

  1. Assistant content is wrapped in {% generation %} markers so TRL's
     assistant_only_loss masks the loss to the tokens the model is responsible for.
     Training on tool output would teach the model to generate cluster state instead of
     querying for it.

     The <|eot_id|> stop token is INSIDE the generation block, and that placement is
     load-bearing for exactly the reason recorded in the ChatML template: with it
     outside, the mask covers the content but not the token that ends the turn, so the
     model is never trained to stop. Teacher forcing hides this in every training metric
     and it appears only at generation time, as turns that ramble to the sampling cap
     without emitting a tool call.

  2. No reasoning block is injected, and the same file is passed to vLLM at serving time
     via --chat-template, so the trained prompt and the served prompt are byte-identical.

  <|begin_of_text|> is deliberately NOT emitted here. Llama 3 tokenizers set
  add_bos_token=True, so the BOS is contributed once at tokenization; emitting it in the
  template as well produces a doubled BOS that shifts every position by one relative to
  what the model saw in pre-training.
-#}
{%- for message in messages -%}
{%- if message['role'] == 'assistant' -%}
{{- '<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n' -}}
{%- generation -%}
{{- message['content'] + '<|eot_id|>' -}}
{%- endgeneration -%}
{%- else -%}
{{- '<|start_header_id|>' + message['role'] + '<|end_header_id|>\n\n' + message['content'] + '<|eot_id|>' -}}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if add_generation_prompt -%}
{{- '<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n' -}}
{%- endif -%}
